          %h2#introduction Introduction
          %p
            The fan theorem is one of the basic principles of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionism"} intuitionism
            that make it more specific (even in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematical
            practice, independent of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/philosophy"} philosophical
            issues) than garden-variety
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale+theory"} locale theory
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-free+topology"} point-free topology
            instead. In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
